  "permissionsMusicOn": "“Follows the music” is switched on now.",
  "permissionsHomeKeyTitle": "Home key",
  "permissionsHomeKeyWhy": "To make the remote's Home key open Home System, Home System becomes the default launcher - or, where that isn't possible (e.g. Fire TV, Google TV), the service “Home System: Home-Taste” is switched on, an accessibility service. The service only sees which app is in front - no screen content, no input, no passwords.",
  "permissionsHomeKeyWhyDashboard": "For the home control the same service also switches the display off and swipes away a lock screen without PIN when the display comes back on.",
  "permissionsCameraTitle": "Camera",
  "permissionsCameraWhy": "For the home control (“switch the display on and off by camera”): the camera only detects whether something moves in front of the device. No pictures are stored or sent anywhere.",
  "permissionsInstallTitle": "Install apps",
  "permissionsInstallWhy": "So that Home System can install its own updates. Android still asks before every update, and Home System never installs any other apps.",
  "permissionsStorageTitle": "Storage",
  "permissionsStorageWhy": "For backups: they're kept in the Download/HomeSystem folder, so they survive uninstalling the app. Home System only reads and writes its own backup files there.",
  "permissionsAllFilesTitle": "All files access",
  "permissionsAllFilesWhy": "Only for backups: new backups in Download/HomeSystem work without it. Home System only needs this access to find an earlier installation's backups after reinstalling - and only reads its own backup files there.",
  "permissionsRecordAudioTitle": "Record audio",
  "permissionsRecordAudioWhy": "Only for the music visualisation (“Follows the music”): it reads the frequency spectrum of the app's own playback. Android calls that “record audio” and mentions the microphone - but the microphone is never used, nothing is recorded or stored.",
  "permissionsUsbTitle": "USB stick for DAB+ and FM",
  "permissionsUsbWhy": "When you plug in an RTL-SDR stick, Android asks once whether Home System may use it. Just choose “OK” (with “Always”, if offered) - Home System only uses that stick.",
  "permissionsNotificationsTitle": "Notifications",
  "permissionsNotificationsWhy": "Home System doesn't ask for them and sends no notifications. While radio or music is playing, Android shows the playback controls - that needs no permission.",
  "permissionsAdvanced": "For advanced users",
  "permissionsSecureSettingsTitle": "Change system settings",
  "permissionsSecureSettingsWhy": "Can only be granted from a computer via adb and isn't needed. With it, Home System switches the Home key service on by itself - also when Android switched it off after an update. Home System changes nothing else with it.",
  "permissionsRestrictedWhy": "From Android 13 on, Android blocks accessibility services of apps that don't come from an app store (“restricted settings”). This command lifts that:",
  "permissionsWizardTitle": "Permissions (optional)",
  "permissionsWizardHint": "Here's what Home System needs which permission for. None of it is required - “Later” always works, and everything can be done later under Settings → System → Permissions.",
